From d24deb6b3239c1ae69a1344cb6e47458ae3b0390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nebur692 <nebur_692@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:31:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-www2-q4fc-65wf: null byte termination in
 dns_get_record() and other network functions [backport to PHP 7.3]

Parse the host/service/protocol names of dns_check_record(), dns_get_mx(),
dns_get_record(), getprotobyname(), getservbyname(), getservbyport(),
inet_pton() and ip2long() as paths ("p"), so that strings with an embedded
NUL byte are rejected instead of being silently truncated by the C
resolver functions.

Origin: php-src ed70b1ea43a9b7ffa2f53b3e5d6ba403f37ae81c (Niels Dossche),
via Remi Collet's 7.4 backport.
Adaptation: dns.c and dns_win32.c use Z_PARAM_ZVAL_DEREF and "z/" in 7.3, so those
hunks were applied by hand. The older ZPP tests still present in 7.3
(getservbyname_variation*, ip2long_variation1, ip.phpt) now expect
"a valid path" instead of "string" in the warning, as ip_x86_64.phpt does
upstream.
---
diff --git a/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/getservbyname_variation1.phpt b/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/getservbyname_variation1.phpt
index 7dd01aab..ac7d9fe0 100644
--- a/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/getservbyname_variation1.phpt
+++ b/ext/standard/tests/general_functions/getservbyname_variation1.phpt
@@ -27,14 +27,14 @@ foreach ( $variation_array as $var ) {
 --EXPECTF--
 *** Test substituting argument 1 with array values ***
 
-Warning: getservbyname() expects parameter 1 to be string, array given in %s on line %d
+Warning: getservbyname() expects parameter 1 to be a valid path, array given in %s on line %d
